  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f306a4e5-5d8a-4b84-8d59-88ed704822bf",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "### Shape of Coherence:\n",
    "coh.shape → (T, F, R, R):\n",
    "\n",
    "T: time bins (based on window + step)\n",
    "\n",
    "F: frequencies (based on multitaper settings)\n",
    "\n",
    "R: brain regions (length of brain_region_dict)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "504a607b-e662-49ee-8406-aa5995e4efd6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "This shape tells us what dimensions our coherence data has:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Dimension | Meaning | Example in our data |\n",
    "|------------|----------|--------------------|\n",
    "| **T = 3600** | Number of time bins | The 30-minute recording was divided into small overlapping windows. Each window is 1 second long, and the analysis moves forward by 0.5 seconds each step. This means every second of the 30-minute recording is covered twice — once starting at the current time, and again starting 0.5 seconds later — giving **3600 small time segments**. |\n",
    "| **F = 500** | Number of frequency points | The analysis looks at 500 frequency values between about 0.5 Hz and 300 Hz. This gives a smooth curve for coherence across the frequency spectrum. |\n",
    "| **R × R = 5 × 5** | Brain region pairs | Coherence is measured between all pairs of regions. Since we have 5 regions (mPFC, MD, NAc, BLA, vHPC), the output is a 5×5 matrix showing coherence between every pair. The diagonal shows self-coherence (always 1.0). |\n",
    "\n",
    "**In short:**  \n",
    "Each 30-minute recording is broken into 3600 overlapping 1-second chunks, and for each chunk, the coherence between every pair of 5 regions is computed across 500 frequencies.  \n",
    "\n",
    "So the data at: coh[t, f, i, j]\n",
    "represents **how synchronized** region *i* and region *j* were at time *t* and frequency *f*.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "465c6ac2-cc5c-4440-8c0f-cf71aab84524",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "(3600, 500, 5, 5)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "d0_44_coh = lfp_collection.recordings[0].coherence\n",
    "print(d0_44_coh.shape)"
   ]
  },
